 @Junior305able  If it's a reference, you're gonna really benefit from undervolting (because it's gonna make the card run cooler). You should watch some videos about how to overclock or underclock the vega 56, youtube has a few, and they explain it well.
It's easy to do, and I don't think you can screw anything up, so you can just mess around and try things. I don't expect a reference 56 to manage a 1650MHz overclock though. I think that might be a bit too much. But, again, do watch some videos here on youtube, there's tricks and tips you're gonna find useful when you're messing around with wattman.


Also, the -75 is just the offset value. Wattman takes the absolute value, so you're gonna put in 1125 if you want a -75 offset. I suggest you start lower than 1125 though, lower clocks, lower voltages, go up from there.
